# LibreWolf kotlin-version-alignment.patch  (Android)
# Owner: LW-M3-12 (align the Kotlin version to Gradle 9.5.1's embedded kotlin-dsl)
#
# THE DEFECT
# ----------
# gradle/libs.versions.toml:8 pins the Kotlin Gradle plugin to 2.3.21, but the
# build runs on Gradle 9.5.1, whose embedded kotlin-dsl and embedded-kotlin
# plugins rely on Kotlin 2.3.20. The build log flags this mismatch itself
# (arm64-v8a.log:802-806):
#
#   The `embedded-kotlin` and `kotlin-dsl` plugins rely on features of Kotlin
#   `2.3.20` that might work differently than in the requested version `2.3.21`.
#   Using the `kotlin-dsl` plugin together with a different Kotlin version ... is
#   not recommended.
#   Applying other version of the `org.jetbrains.kotlin.jvm` plugin in the build
#   and/or adding dependencies to different versions of the Kotlin Standard
#   Library can cause incompatibilities.
#
# The observed failure is a Kotlin-plugin-internal build-service registration
# type conflict on :geckoview:compileDebugKotlin (a DEBUG task run by
# `mach android export` for geckoview API extraction):
#
#   Could not load the value of field `__buildFusService__` of task
#   `:geckoview:compileDebugKotlin` of type
#   `org.jetbrains.kotlin.gradle.tasks.KotlinCompile`.
#   Cannot set the value of a property of type
#   org.jetbrains.kotlin.gradle.plugin.statistics.BuildFusService using a
#   provider of type
#   org.jetbrains.kotlin.gradle.plugin.statistics.FlowActionBuildFusService.
#
# THE FAULT IS INTERMITTENT - attribution is unproven
# ----------------------------------------------------
# It is NOT deterministic. On 2026-08-22 the x86_64 pass hit this exact fault
# and then PASSED on a later run with no version change (the failing log was
# overwritten by the successful rerun). On 2026-08-24 the arm64-v8a and
# armeabi-v7a first passes hit it in clean fresh outdirs (empty
# GRADLE_USER_HOME, no prior pass to leave state). So it is a real,
# sometimes-reproducible fault, but a single green pass does not prove it is
# fixed and a single red pass does not prove this alignment caused it. The
# shared-GRADLE_USER_HOME / pass-order hypothesis was explicitly falsified by
# the 2026-08-24 clean-first-pass failures.
#
# THE FIX (defensible correctness, NOT a proven fault fix)
# ---------------------------------------------------------
# Align the Kotlin version to 2.3.20 to match Gradle 9.5.1's embedded
# kotlin-dsl / embedded-kotlin, removing the version mismatch the build log
# itself flags as "not recommended" and "can cause incompatibilities." The
# version mismatch is real regardless of whether this specific fault is
# attributable to it. This patch removes a real Kotlin/Gradle version mismatch
# that is a known source of Kotlin-plugin-internal incompatibilities; it does
# NOT claim the intermittent fault is fixed. Evidence is reported as
# "mismatch removed", NOT "fault fixed"; the attribution is unproven.
#
# SCOPE / ORDERING
# ----------------
# One line in gradle/libs.versions.toml [versions]. no-adjust and no-gms also
# carry a hunk in gradle/libs.versions.toml but only in the [versions] /
# [libraries] Google-dependency sections (lines 56+); neither touches the
# `kotlin =` line (line 8) or the [versions] Kotlin block, so this hunk is
# order-free against both. The two order-free pairs (kotlin-version-alignment
# + no-adjust, kotlin-version-alignment + no-gms) are declared in
# docs/android/AGENTS.md and scripts/check-patch-order.py.

--- a/gradle/libs.versions.toml
+++ b/gradle/libs.versions.toml
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@
 
 # Kotlin
 coroutines = "1.11.0"
-kotlin = "2.3.21"
+kotlin = "2.3.20"
 serialization = "1.11.0"
 
 # AndroidX
